# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: runner-availability-gating — auto-start native (macOS/Windows) jobs only when their runner is online
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: RUNNER_STATUS_TOKEN (a CI/CD variable pjb must add)
#+BRANCH: feature-runner-availability-gating

* Context

The macOS/Windows CI runners are intermittent laptops. Native jobs
therefore can't simply be `when: on_success`: when the runner is offline
they pile up as stuck-pending jobs and (if not allow_failure) redden the
pipeline. Until now the manual jobs (vendor:probes, verify:*, pathname:*,
benchmark, release) never auto-ran even when the runner WAS online, and
the test:* jobs auto-ran on master but piled up when the runner was down.

pjb's request: two "is-the-runner-up?" probes, from which the native jobs
depend so they launch AUTOMATICALLY when the runner is online, and fall
back to MANUAL when it is offline (manual trigger always available).

* Problem / GitLab constraint

`rules:` are evaluated at pipeline-CREATION time and cannot see a probe
job's runtime result in the same pipeline. So "on_success if online else
manual" via rules needs the runner status known at creation — impossible
for a same-pipeline probe. Two viable shapes:
  - a parent→child pipeline (detect job passes MACOS/WINDOWS=online var to
    a child whose native jobs use rules on it) — clean, but moves every
    native job into a child YAML (big refactor; breaks parent↔child
    needs:/artifacts);
  - an ORCHESTRATOR that keeps every native job `when: manual` (so offline
    == the manual fallback) and, from the always-on Linux runner, `play`s
    the manual jobs whose runner is online.

* Implemented (orchestrator, chosen for zero disruption)

- scripts/ci-autostart-native-runners.py + the `.pre` job
  `autostart:native-runners` in .gitlab-ci.yml. It queries
  GET /projects/:id/runners?tag_list={macos,windows} for an online runner,
  then `play`s this pipeline's manual jobs carrying that tag. Excludes
  release:* / benchmark:*. FAIL-SAFE: no token / API error => plays
  nothing => every native job stays manual (today's behaviour). Validated:
  the runners API filters by tag and reports online/offline correctly;
  glab ci lint is green.

* To activate (pjb)

1. Add a CI/CD variable RUNNER_STATUS_TOKEN = a project access token with
   `api` scope (playing a job is a write; read_api is not enough). Masked;
   protected if auto-start should only happen on protected refs (note: an
   MR pipeline from a non-protected branch then won't get the token, so its
   native jobs stay manual — acceptable, or make it unprotected).
2. Watch a pipeline: online runners => their native manual jobs auto-start;
   offline => they stay manual.

* Follow-ups

- Phase 2 (optional): flip test:* (.platform-test-common) and the encoding
  jobs from `on_success` to `when: manual` so they too fall back to manual
  (no stuck-pending) when the runner is offline, and are auto-started by
  this orchestrator when online. Deferred until the token is confirmed, so
  master test coverage is not left manual-without-auto in the interim.
- Tune SKIP_PREFIXES (or add a per-job marker) if some native jobs should
  NOT auto-run on every push (e.g. the AutoCAD probes while unlicensed).

* Acceptance criteria

- With RUNNER_STATUS_TOKEN set: native manual jobs whose runner is online
  start automatically; offline ones stay manual; pipeline never reddens or
  piles up because of an offline laptop.
- Without the token: identical to today (all native jobs manual).
